**Equivalent Java `switch` statement:**
```java
char tariffSlab = 'C';

switch (tariffSlab) {
    case 'D':
        System.out.println("Domestic Residential: ₹ 5.50 / Unit");
        break;
    case 'C':
        System.out.println("Commercial Enterprise: ₹ 9.00 / Unit");
        break;
    case 'I':
        System.out.println("Heavy Industrial Factory: ₹ 12.50 / Unit");
        break;
    default:
        System.out.println("Standard Public Utility");
        break;
}
```

**Answer:**
- **Method Overloading:** Defining multiple methods in the same class with the same name but **different parameter signatures** (compile-time polymorphism).
- **Example:**
```java
public class BillingCalculator {
    // Overloaded method for standard single item
    public double calculateTotal(double price) {
        return price * 1.18; // 18% GST
    }

    // Overloaded method for multiple quantity with discount
    public double calculateTotal(double price, int quantity, double discountRate) {
        double base = price * quantity;
        return (base - (base * discountRate)) * 1.18;
    }
}
```

